
AAC Huffman tables
------------------
internal/media/aac_tables_gen.go contains the AAC (ISO/IEC 14496-3) spectral and
scalefactor Huffman codebooks, extracted from the read-only data of FFmpeg's
libavcodec 6.0 (libavcodec.so.60.31.102). FFmpeg's libavcodec is licensed under
the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The repository
owner accepted this licensing for these tables. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.

HE-AAC (SBR and parametric stereo) tables
-----------------------------------------
internal/media/sbr_tables_gen.go contains the SBR (spectral band replication)
and PS (parametric stereo) constant tables of ISO/IEC 14496-3: the Huffman
codebooks for envelope, noise floor, IID, ICC, IPD and OPD data, the 640 tap
QMF prototype window, the noise table, the SBR start frequency offset table
and the PS band mapping and dequantisation constants. Like the AAC codebooks
above they were extracted from the read-only data of FFmpeg's libavcodec 6.0
(libavcodec.so.60.31.102), which is licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later; the repository owner accepted this
licensing for these tables too. The generator script verifies every codebook
(prefix free, Kraft sum 1) and the symmetry of the QMF window. The decoding
algorithms in sbr.go, sbr_qmf.go and ps.go follow the standard and reproduce
the behaviour, including implementation details, of FFmpeg's libavcodec
aacsbr / aacps decoders (LGPL-2.1-or-later), against whose output they were
verified. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.

Opus decoding
-------------
Opus decoding uses github.com/thesyncim/gopus (BSD-3-Clause).

AV1 decoding
------------
internal/media/av1 is a pure-Go implementation of the AV1 decoding process
written from the AV1 Bitstream & Decoding Process Specification (Alliance for
Open Media, https://aomedia.org/license/). Its constant tables
(internal/media/av1/tables_gen.go, cdf_gen.go, transform_gen.go) were
extracted by script from the text of that specification and cross-checked
against the read-only data of libaom. The test fixtures were encoded with
libaom, SVT-AV1 and rav1e, and the expected output hashes come from dav1d.

